  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Select saute setting on a 6-qt. electric pressure cooker and adjust for high heat.",
      "group": null
    },
    {
      "text": "Add 2 teaspoons oil. Sprinkle beef with salt and pepper. Use the saute feature to brown the beef for added flavor. Brown meat in batches, adding oil as needed. Transfer meat to a bowl.",
      "group": null
    },
    {
      "text": "Add wine to cooker, stirring to loosen browned bits.",
      "group": null
    },
    {
      "text": "Return beef to cooker; add mushrooms, onion, broth and Worcestershire sauce. Lock lid; make sure vent is closed.",
      "group": null
    },
    {
      "text": "Select manual setting; adjust pressure to high and set time for 15 minutes. When finished cooking, quick-release pressure according to manufacturer's directions.",
      "group": null
    },
    {
      "text": "Select saute setting and adjust for high heat; bring liquid to a boil. In a small bowl, mix cornstarch and water until smooth; gradually stir into beef mixture. Cook and stir until sauce is thickened, 1-2 minutes.",
      "group": null
    },
    {
      "text": "The next day, stir a little heavy cream or sour cream into leftover sauce and (carb alert) serve over mashed potatoes, rice or pasta.",
      "group": null
    }
  ],
